  <channel>
    <title>InvestPR Media Monitoring</title>
    <link>https://bestedc.github.io/ipr-digest-feed/digest.xml</link>
    <description>This period produced no new investment announcements — no FDI, expansions, facility openings, or federal awards appeared in the candidate set. The most actionable item is renewed pressure from the Centro Unido de Detallistas to eliminate the inventory tax and speed permitting, both recurring friction points cited by site-selection consultants evaluating Puerto Rico. On the demand side, the Housing Finance Authority is promoting homebuyer programs (~$18 million disbursed to 620 families) against estimated unmet demand above 30,000 units, underscoring a persistent housing-supply constraint on workforce attraction. Remaining coverage was opinion-driven — a critique of permitting centralization and an analysis flagging thin margins and high loan-to-deposit ratios at local cooperatives — worth monitoring as a credit-conditions signal but not a deal-flow indicator.</description>
    <language>en-us</language>
    <lastBuildDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 20:57:07 +0000</lastBuildDate>
